.policy "ruff-f701-break-outside-loop" revision 2
.description "Keep break inside a for or while loop body; outside one (including a loop's else block) it is a Python syntax error."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff F701 (pyflakes): `break` with no enclosing loop body in its own def, class or module. CPython rejects the
// file. A loop's `else` clause is not inside the loop, and a def or class in between hides an outer loop.
//   for x in xs: pass
//   else: break              ← F701
//   while c: break           not reported
#include "python/pyflakes.rr"
//   outside_loop(s)  break/continue s has no loop body around it in its def, class or module

.violation F701(at: node) code "F701" "`break` outside loop"
    suppress ruff "F701"
F701(s) :- kind(s, "break_statement"), outside_loop(s).
